WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.290
Monitor coming through. What's going on-

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.040
Sis!

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:08.960
Hina!

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.500
What are you doing here?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.460
Sis, Rinko-chan!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.990
Let's do a double culture festival
with our two schools!

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.460
Student Council

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.420
A double culture festival?

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.790
Yeah, with Haneoka.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.670
Remember how you guys performed with Afterglow
in the market the other day?

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.500
Yeah...

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.430
Well, that got me thinking!

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.260
That's what prompted this?
It doesn't even make sense.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.460
But...

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:09.060
Besides, you can't just show up at another person's
school without making an appointment.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.960
And during lunch, nonetheless.
You still have class after this, don't you?

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:17.780
Sorry. I thought lunch would be
the easiest time to see you.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.710
So, what did you mean by
double culture festival exactly?

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.580
Well, we could hold them on the same day
and do some programs together.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.960
Wouldn't it be boppin' if the visitors
could zip back and forth?

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.710
Zipping... bopping...

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.380
Ichigaya-san, you can just ignore her.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.880
What do you think, Rinko-chan?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.580
What?

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.750
Are you for it?

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.960
Uh...

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.890
You should be the one to decide
as student council president.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.000
M-me?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.460
Time for a live show meeting!

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.040
How about our new song?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.040
Maybe we should pick a date first.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.920
We can't really plan without that,
and it has to work for everyone.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.960
That's true.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.210
How about summer break?

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.880
Kokoron's going on a trip.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.250
Chisato-senpai and the others
said they're free in June.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.250
They're gonna talk to 
their management about it.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.960
PasuPare agreed to perform?!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.750
That's crazy! How'd you convince them?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.960
It's a secret.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.000
They said Galaxy should be open whenever.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.540
Then... how about the last Saturday of June?

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.590
A month from now... That's not a lot of time.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.750
But it'll push us to create something
that much more fantastic.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:26.350
Yeah!

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.680
Are we good with that date?
We'll need to confirm with everyone.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.170
Plus, prep for the culture 
festival starts soon too.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.080
We're gonna be busier than ever!

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.630
I don't want to think about it...

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.210
You've got this.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:41.330
Oh! The festival will be our
one-year anniversary as PoPiPa!

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.000
That's right!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.830
Last year's culture festival was the first time
the five of us performed together, huh.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.290
Yep.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.580
Should we celebrate?!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.130
Celebrate how...?

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.170
I want to perform.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.290
A live show?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.090
An anniversary concert.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.050
I love it.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.090
H-hold on! What about 
the self-sponsored show?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.330
We'll do both!

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.220
Huh?!

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.000
When we performed at the 
market the other day,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.600
I realized that we gain so much
by playing live in front of people.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.670
Maybe so, but...

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.130
I think I want to do it too.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:19.170
I know it'll be tough, but there's just something
special about culture festivals, you know?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.790
And I want to be able to play 
the whole set this time.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.330
Oh, fine!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.330
Yay!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.790
Thanks!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.790
We've gotta prep for all 
of this simultaneously!

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.540
We're setting schedules.
Not a second goes to waste!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.380
Yep.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.840
Yep! So, back to that new song!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.840
We need to create a set list too.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.790
And a time table, and costumes...

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.630
Ugh! Come on, one at a time!

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.080
Hello? Rin-rin!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.960
Hi, Ako-chan. I can hear you fine.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.750
That's a relief. It says you're offline,
so I was starting to wonder.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.460
Sorry. I've just been thinking 
about the culture festival...

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:13.540
Oh! Hina-chan was talking 
about that at the assembly.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.450
Angel Princess Ako

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.960
Everyone!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.420
How'd you like to team up with
Hanasakigawa for the festival?!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.880
Everybody sounded excited.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.210
C-crazy, huh...

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.140
I think a double culture 
festival sounds like fun,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.330
but when I think about making
such an important decision, I just...

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.930
I'm all for it!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:37.290
With you and Hina-chin in charge,
I'm sure the festival's gonna be super fun!

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.750
Y-you think so?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.960
Well... it's worth a try...

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.460
Yesss!

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.960
I'm so excited for this!

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:50.020
Ako-chan, you know,

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.990
I signed on as president so that I could 
get used to speaking in front of people...

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:59.630
but now that I'm here, I want to help make this year
as amazing as I can for everyone.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.880
Rin-rin, you already do 
that as your game avatar!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.960
W-well, games are different from real life,
so I don't really know how I'll do...

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.100
But I want to try.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.350
Sis!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.460
Sis! The double festival is a go!

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.040
How many times do I have 
to tell you to knock?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.960
I already heard about it.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.420
This is so exciting!

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.290
Hina.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.960
You'd better make sure you watch closely
and keep everyone in line.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:34.920
Okay! We can patrol the festival together
so you can keep me from doing anything stupid!

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.000
Uh-huh.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.120
What?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.620
Asahi Bathhouse

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.290
What?! PoPiPa are performing 
at the festival?!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.540
They're gonna try and do both
their show and the festival.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.550
My sister's been practicing nonstop.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.420
I was excited for the 
double festival as it is!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.960
And now a show too?!

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.000
I have to get a front row seat...

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.580
B-but I also want to help out...

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.210
Don't forget about the 
program for our own class.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.290
Are you gonna perform, Rokka?

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:01.380
What?

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:05.920
I kind of want to, but I still
haven't found any band members...

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:07.830
But I will!

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.500
I'll find them somehow, 
before the festival...

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.290
I hope so.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.210
I wonder why you can't find anyone.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:17.380
I'm sure it's mostly because I'm dreadful...

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.500
PoPiPa's not PoPiPa without 
all five members, right?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.790
I hope I can find people
I really click with like that, too...

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.250
Oh! Is that me?

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.290
Hello? Asahi speaking.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.040
Really?! Yes!

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.630
I'll be right there! Thank you!

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.970
PoPiPa are at Galaxy right now!

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:45.460
Uh-huh... What about me?

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.920
The last Saturday of June, right? That works!

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.130
Thank goodness.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.710
Can we rent the previous evening, too?

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.330
Sure, of course.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.250
Miko, I'll pencil them in, okay?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.420
All right.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.500
Is Galaxy doing okay?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.920
Your schedule's wide open.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.960
It looks like there are a 
few things on weeknights.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.750
What made you choose Galaxy?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.510
I really like it, but there 
are plenty of others...

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.180
It's because you're here, Lock!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.540
You already know us really well.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.560
And it's easier to visualize the stage
since we've already performed here before.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.170
Lock?

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.080
I'm just so happy...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.080
O-okay...

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.320
O-Tae-chan.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.460
These are really well-used.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.170
If there's anything you guys
want to do onstage, let me know.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.960
I can talk to the owner and manager.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.040
Thanks!

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:43.920
See you soon!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.000
Owner?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.460
Yo.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.630
I didn't know you were here, Masuki-chan.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.050
It was kinda loud out here,
so I just read some manga in the dressing room.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.750
Some girls came in that'll 
be performing here soon.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:57.890
Huh.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.470
Maybe renovating this place 
was worth it after all.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.500
I'll be here for around two hours.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.330
Did you get a support drumming gig?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.790
Yeah, but not as support.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:08.630
What?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.710
I got scouted.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:14.420
One more month until our 
self-sponsored show...

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.330
Bet it's gonna go by fast.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.420
Yeah. But we've got the festival before that!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.670
We need to remember to get 
the application forms.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.370
Oh, and create a set list 
and plan everything out!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.540
Let's divide up the work. Okay? Hm?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.670
O-Tae?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.830
What?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.710
Are you tired? Sleepy?

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:35.630
No, I've just got a lot on my mind.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:38.720
Do you two feel like 
you're lacking something?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:39.630
Huh?

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.670
Allowance money.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:42.670
Time?

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:45.780
For me, it's... experience.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.060
Hm?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.920
Practice sessions aren't enough.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:53.790
I want to feel the music and how it's being
conveyed to the audience as I'm playing.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.000
You mean playing live?

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.820
Yeah. I'd love to be able to play again,
at least once, before our show.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.240
How about a daily mini show?

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.830
Might be hard to get an audience...

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.130
True.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.330
It's fine.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:10.790
We can start now.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.540
Street performing?! No way!

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.040
Have you done this before?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.510
A bit, a long time ago.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.080
There are so many people.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.790
Yeah, but no one knows us here.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.940
We'll have to grab their 
attention with music.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:41.830
Did I give you chills?

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.130
Yeah! Look at these goosebumps!

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:46.420
I should have brought more amps.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.540
I'll sing! How about you, Rimi-rin?

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.290
What?

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.750
All right. "My Heart is a Chocolate Cornet!"

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:54.460
Huh?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.460
Chocolate cornet!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.130
Huh?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.000
HaneSaki Fest
Haneoka Girls' Academy x Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy
Double Culture Festival

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.830
Booths
Bratwurst  Hot Dogs  Takoyaki  Yakisoba  Okonomiyaki  Karaage
Hash Browns  Crepes  Churros  Shaved Ice  Cotton Candy  Bubble Tea
Bushido Croquette  Tea House  Café Cat Café  and more

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:03.890
Special Events
Haneoka Girls' Academy Auditorium
6/8 (Sat) Double Theater Production, "Macbeth"
6/9 (Sun) Double Culture Festival Anniversary Concert
Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy Gymnasium
6/8 (Sat) Dance Battle
6/9 (Sun) School Band Jazz Session, "Take the ARAKABA Train"

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:03.890
After all events are over, a camp fire closing ceremony will be held.
*Please make sure you receive a stamp on your hand (washable) upon arrival.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.680
Street performing?!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.290
Why that all of a sudden?

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.500
It's training.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.540
Intensive training for our show!

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.750
I took a video.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:14.790
I wanna see!

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:17.830
Whoa, you're singing.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:18.960
Ooh!

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:22.210
Want to see one where Rimi-rin's singing?

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.000
Yeah!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:23.830
Wha...?

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.580
This is embarrassing...

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.670
Were you shy about singing, Rimi?

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:29.960
Mhmm.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:35.580
But I want to learn to be less nervous,
so I'm glad you invited me.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.040
O-Tae-chan?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.250
You're too cute.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.040
Seems like it feels good, singing outside.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.500
Want to train too, Saaya?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.540
Yeah, let's train!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.580
We've got work to do before that!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.000
That's right!

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.960
We should probably use
summer constellations for the planetarium...

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.500
I'm not talking about our class program!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.790
What about the new song?!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:12:00.540
You said you were gonna write up a description
about what you were thinking.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.990
Well, I did start on it...

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.210
Do it now!

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.130
Okay!

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.670
We should do what we can for now, too.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.580
Yep.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.710
That was nerve-wrecking...

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.830
Shirokane-san, are you in here?

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.210
O-over here.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.010
I had a feeling you'd be here.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.030
It c-calms me down...

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.630
I'm going back to student council.

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.290
Um, Eikawa-san?

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:31.420
Thank you for coming to the 
double council meeting.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:34.380
Thank YOU for looking after 
my trouble-maker sister.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.980
Sh-she hasn't been a trouble-maker.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.460
Hina-san has a great imagination,
and she's so determined.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:41.920
Yeah...

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.630
Hazawa-san has been working really hard too.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.280
Double culture festival?
- Hanasakigawa and Haneoka?
- Same day with mixed programming??
- Visitors could zip back and forth???

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.410
I wonder where my sister's classroom is...

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.920
I'm really busy prepping for the culture festival again today.
My classmates and I have been working super hard.
I feel like I want to do something extra since it'll be
my last high school festival, though.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.420
Something amazing that 
we'll remember forever.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.420
...we'll remember forever, heart emoji.
Something amazing that we'll remember forever.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:58.380
...we'll remember forever, heart emoji.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.420
Hina-chan! Management 
hasn't checked this yet-

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.960
I already read it.
Hina-chan! Management hasn't checked this yet-

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.050
What are we gonna remember forever?

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.290
I'm still thinking.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.890
I really wanted to perform live with PasuPare,
but our management said no.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.330
Really?

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.640
Well, why don't you put together a new band?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.460
What?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.730
Won't it be fine as long 
as it's not PasuPare?

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.410
You can just perform as a plain 
old high schooler, right?

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.040
Plain old Aya...

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.110
That might work!

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.250
Boppin'!

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:32.490
Remind me, why are we doing this?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.160
'Cause you're my friends...

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.580
But I'm a member of PasuPare, and so are you.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.330
Hey, which one's my sister's desk?

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.080
She's right up front.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.040
Hina-chan's the producer.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.330
Producer?

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.720
Someone who guides the band's direction.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.750
They support the band as a business partner,
part of which is bringing in listeners.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.420
Want to do it with us, Kanon-chan?

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.500
You work at the same 
place as Aya-chan, right?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.420
Huh? A band, huh...

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.630
Kanon, you're allowed to say no-

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:03.830
Yeah, let's do it.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:04.460
What?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.210
Really?!

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:06.250
Are you sure?!

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.960
Hina's not twisting your 
arm or anything, is she?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.960
You can tell me the truth, Kanon!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:11.920
It's fine...

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.290
Chisato-chan...

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.130
Let's rev up the engines!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.540
Welcome!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.380
Lisa-chi!

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.330
Thanks in advance!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.050
Hina-senpai!

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.790
I finally found you!

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.380
Wanna join us, Tsugu-chan?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.580
S-sure!

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.580
Join what?

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.140
Haneoka Girls' Academy

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.600
So we've got...

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.080
Aya-chan on vocals,

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.520
Lisa-chi on bass,

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.980
Kanon-chan on drums,

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.460
Tsugu-chan on keyboard,

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:49.630
and me as guitarist, producer,
and student council president!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.960
That's quite the title.

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.250
Guess we already have our members...

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.420
Is this supposed to be a band?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:59.130
Aya-chan said she wanted to put one together!

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.830
Thanks again!

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.800
It's only temporary,
but I hope we can have a lot of fun!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.960
Sounds good!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.130
Let's do it.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.170
Y-yeah...

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.830
Coming in.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:13.260
It's us, Afterglow.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.600
Can I help you?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.040
Uh...

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.330
We came to talk to Hina-san.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.540
Can you stop bothering 
Tsugumi like this, please?

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.330
You're dragging her all over the place
when she's trying to prep for the festival.

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.540
Ran-chan...

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.540
If you think we're just gonna
let this go on, you're mistak-

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.350
If you think we're just gonna
let this go on, you're mistak-

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.380
So you'll help us, then?

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.750
Yay! Thank you!

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.210
Yipee!

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.630
Tomoe, do something.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.460
Me?!

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.830
She doesn't get it.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.210
Ran, it's a lost cause...

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:42.070
Hina-senpai's no joke.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:45.250
Now I can pass the baton to you, Moca-chan!

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.250
Huh?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.630
The five of you!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:52.380
I want you to be our special 
double festival band!

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.330
What?!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:55.920
You'll be great!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.040
A culture festival concert?

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.920
We're performing as a session band.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.290
Is that okay?

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.940
As long as it doesn't affect 
Roselia, it's fine by me.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.040
Hey, just out of curiosity...

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.130
What do you think about Roselia
performing at the festival?

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:13.920
What?

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.420
We could totally rile 
up the crowd as Roselia.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.580
It would be hard to forget 
something like that!

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:23.470
I don't create music for the 
sake of making memories.

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:26.380
Y-yeah, you're right...

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.920
I'm gonna go reserve our next session.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.550
This is a mess...

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.140
You don't have to rush.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:40.630
What kind of show do you want to put on?

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.460
That's right. This song will be for
our self-sponsored show, huh.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:46.750
Maybe you can try starting from there.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.420
I want it to feel like PoPiPa.

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.040
What do you mean?

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:58.290
Well, I kinda realized after watching Hello Happy
and all the other bands perform...

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:04.370
It's the five of us, Rimi-rin, Saaya, O-Tae, Arisa,
and I, that make our shows what they are!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.630
Because it's us five.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.710
Sounds like a good start!

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.880
Yeah! All right, time to write!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.710
Everybody sparkling...

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:23.750
What does it mean to "feel like PoPiPa?"

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.270
Thank you!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.540
Kasumi
Got an idea for our new song.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.870
Fun and sparkly /
We're all connected /
Our music is our bond /
We've been through tough times /
But today is the greatest!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.120
Let our sounds ring together /
So they reach everyone /
Even if we lose sight of each other or drift apart /
We can find each other again...
Something like that?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.920
We'll find each other again...

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:05.000
I Won't Cry, I Won't Cry

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:29.810
Lay.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.460
I'm home.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:38.130
Hana-chan...

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.170
let's go!

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:41.990
Okay!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.960
Man, that felt great.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.000
Yeah.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.580
Welcome home, Lay.

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:01.130
Last I saw you was elementary 
school... six years?

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.170
It doesn't feel like it's been that long.

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:07.720
We sang that song together
before I moved away, didn't we?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:11.890
Yeah, at the park near the music school.

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:17.000
That was the first time I'd ever
played music with another person.

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:20.920
When did you move back?

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.330
Beginning of spring.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.790
I wanted to come visit you sooner...

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:29.920
When I dropped by your house, they said
you've been performing in front of the station lately.

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.750
You've got even more rabbits now, huh.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.880
I need to hurry up and
build Hanazono Land for them all...

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.250
You haven't changed a bit, have you?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.750
Have you changed, Lay?

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.710
Hmm... I dunno.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.960
Oh, I play bass now.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.080
Bass?

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:49.670
I promised you that one day
we'd form a band together, didn't I?

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:56.710
Lately, I've been performing as a
support musician and singing for work.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.460
Are you in a band now?

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:00.330
Yeah.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.400
With my friends from school.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:03.830
I see.

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:08.580
I'd be stoaked if you'd join my band anyways.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.460
What?

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:15.080
I think you'll understand 
once you listen to my band.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.210
Sweet! Excellent!

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.380
Congratulations, Masking!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:34.790
CHU2-sama, is Masking Masuki-sama's
new name or something?

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:37.140
Yes! It's sick, right?

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:42.420
This crazy lone wolf is about to become
my greatest drummer ever.

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.330
Pareo!

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:44.920
Yes, CHU2-sama!

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.360
Here's your jerkey.

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.830
Just you wait, Roselia...

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:54.420
My all-star band is about 
to explode onto the scene!

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:38.640
Next episode: You're Not Alone
